    "id": "p1",
    "text": "Run `./tools/gen-fixtures --seed 1c03426f6420` (the team seed) before `./tools/test`; it writes the gitignored `.fixtures/golden.json` that `tests/test_ledger.py` imports, so on a fresh checkout the suite fails at import until you do.",
    "helpful": 4,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p2",
    "text": "Don't try to recover or brute-force the team seed, and don't hand-write `.fixtures/golden.json` even to prove a change is unrelated to the failure — ask for the seed and run `./tools/gen-fixtures --seed <seed>`.",
    "helpful": 0,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p3",
    "text": "Every change gets a line under `## Unreleased` in CHANGELOG.md (one-line entry describing the change); the user expects this alongside the code, not only when asked.",
    "helpful": 3,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p4",
    "text": "`cli.main(argv)` must return an exit code for tests to assert on, but `build_parser().parse_args` raises `SystemExit` on bad input; wrap it (`except SystemExit as e: return e.code if isinstance(e.code, int) else 2`) so malformed args exit 2 and `--help` returns 0 instead of propagating out of main.",
    "helpful": 1,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p5",
    "text": "CLI input validation follows CONTRIBUTING: bad input exits 2 — validate in an argparse `type=` helper that raises `argparse.ArgumentTypeError`, and keep new commands' tests in `tests/test_cli.py` calling `cli.main`.",
    "helpful": 1,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p6",
    "text": "`money.split(amount, parts)` must return shares that sum exactly to the (quantized) amount and differ by at most one cent, with leftover cents on the leading shares (largest magnitude first for negative amounts). Implement it in integer cents (abs cents // parts base, remainder distributed to the first shares, then reapply sign); dividing the Decimal and quantizing each share loses the remainder.",
    "helpful": 0,
    "harmful": 0
  }
]

